(Aborted is the shell reporting SIGABRT; its exact wording differs between shells.) The abort is not a panic. catch_unwind cannot stop it, and destructors do not run. Vec::try_reserve is available on Vec&lt;T, A&gt; (it has been stable since 1.57 and works with any allocator), so the fallible path is to reserve before you push and handle the TryReserveError. Note too that 128 bytes of real data cost 224 bytes of arena, because the 32- and 64-byte blocks left behind by each growth step are never reused.


